RF.put("questb:b78",{"8638":{"id":8638,"t":"Deathdealer's Vest","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the the Carapace of the Old God, 2 Idols of Strife, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Honored reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nCarapace of the Old God C'Thun in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Strife Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 9000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The unmentionable Old God slowly awakens from his slumber beneath Ahn'Qiraj. The terrible fate that awaits Azeroth could come in days or years; time has no meaning for beings of his power.\nWhen the stars are favorable, he will lash out against all living beings with terrible wrath. You must find him before then and find a way to bring his existence to an end.\nDo this and bring me a piece of his husk. I shall grant you armor no mortal has ever worn... armor fit for one who has slain a god!","rew":"You will receive:\nDeathdealer's Vest\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"At his dwelling in Ahn'Qiraj, dread C'Thun awaits in slumber.","done":"I did not expect you to return from your attempt, ‹name›.\nYou've fulfilled a destiny greater than that of most immortal beings.\nBy slaying C'Thun you've not only saved all of Azeroth, you've also tipped the scales of cosmic events beyond your comprehension.\nAccept this breastplate as a symbol of the glory and burden that will come as a consequence of your actions.\nMay its power aid you in the challenges that await you, god-slayer!\nStart Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Vethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Rogue Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8638\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Deathdealer's Vest this quest\nBring the the Carapace of the Old God, 2 Idols of Strife, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Vethsera inside Ahn'Qiraj.\nVethsera Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8558":{"id":8558,"t":"Sickle of Unyielding Strength","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Spiked Hilt, 2 Alabaster Idols, 5 Crystal Scarabs and 5 Stone Scarabs to Warden Haro in Silithus. You must also attain Exalted reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Spiked Hilt Ossirian the Unscarred 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Alabaster Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Crystal Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 42000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The Qiraji and their servants wield items made with the rarest and finest materials: bones from gargantuan ancient creatures, gems from the depths of the earth, metals pure and strong.\nJust the sight of Qiraji artifacts fills me with an urge to practice my craft with their shattered and smelted pieces. Prove your allegiance to the Circle, ‹name›, and I will make you a powerful weapon from the finest Qiraji materials.","rew":"You will receive:\nSickle of Unyielding Strength\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the components I require, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹class›. This is a masterwork hilt... the balance is perfect.\nTake your weapon, ‹name›. Wield it with great confidence and vanquish our enemies!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.1,"y":38.9,"n":"Warden Haro","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8398":{"id":8398,"t":"Claiming Arathi Basin","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Arathi Basin Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor","desc":"Winning a war is about more than just outsmarting and outfighting your opponent. Victory often comes down to simply producing more than your enemy.\nWhat we have in Arathi Basin is a sizeable supply of resources for whichever side manages to claim it first.\nIf the Alliance comes out victorious, it'll mean more swords and pikes for our troops. If the Horde were to win, those swords and pikes would still get made, they'd just be pointed at us! Now is the time to help the Alliance in Arathi Basin, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 3,300\n+50 reputation with The League of Arathor","back":"Tell me, what are the news from the front?","done":"Good work, soldier! Keep it up and we'll have the Horde running all the way back to Orgrimmar.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"1918":{"id":1918,"t":"The Befouled Element","lv":27,"min":23,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Befouled Water Globe to Mastok Wrilehiss at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.\nBefouled Water Globe Tideress\nProvided: Befouled Water Globe","desc":"The slain elemental has produced an intensely glowing globe of water. The contents of the globe are, at best, disgusting. It would be safe to assume that whatever has befouled the water of Mystral Lake is most likely present in the water of the globe.\nIt's not exactly common knowledge who might be interested in such a find; perhaps the person who originally sent you out to the lake, Mastok Wrilehiss at Splintertree Post, might have an idea.","rew":"Experience: 550\n+25 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Yeah, what do you need?","done":"You find a nasty ball of water and decide to bring it to me? Who am I, the Earthen Ring or something?\nActually, that does give me an idea... perhaps you do need the Earthen Ring for this. I mean, if it helps clear up the situation at the lake for good, then I'm all for it.\nYou know who the Earthen Ring are, ‹name›?","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":73.7,"y":60,"n":"Mastok Wrilehiss","e":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"1038":{"id":1038,"t":"Velinde's Effects","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Search through Velinde's chest for her journal, then return it along with the key to Thyn'tel Bladeweaver in Darnassus.\nVelinde's Journal Velinde's Locker\nVelinde's Key\nProvided: Velinde's Key","desc":"The Tome of Mel'Thandris showed you this? I suppose there would be little harm in allowing you to examine her belongings. This key will allow you to open the chest where we stored her things in the Sentinels' bunkhouse. She kept a journal of her duties, if there is anything to be learned, it will be from that.\nI should tell you, the Sentinels believe that she had her own reasons for leaving, and expect that she could return at any time. The priestess has done much in the past to earn our trust.","rew":"Experience: 600\n+25 reputation with Darnassus","back":"What'd you find out?","done":"It seems that Velinde's disappearance is more troubling than it originally appeared. Even still, I cannot believe that she has come to a bad end. Perhaps it would be beneficial for us to make contact with her.\n‹name›, since you have shown a vested interest in this matter, I would like to enlist your aid.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":61.8,"y":39.2,"n":"Thyn'tel Bladeweaver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"3518":{"id":3518,"t":"Delivery to Magatha","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Tablet of Beth'Amara to Magatha in Thunder Bluff.\nTablet of Beth'Amara Tablet of Beth'Amara\nProvided: Tablet of Beth'Amara","desc":"The first tablet goes to a tauren female... one called Magatha. She is among the elders in Thunder Bluff, and is one of the proponents of the alliance between the tauren and the Forsaken. She, more than anyone among the elders, feels the tauren and their ways can help the Forsaken find a path back to being human.\nBring her the Tablet of Beth'Amara. The tablet may be the link she needs in finding a way to help the Forsaken... or so she claims.","rew":"Experience: 2,550","back":"Yes, ‹name›. What can I do for you? I have many matters I must attend to, so please, be quick.","done":"Ah, at long last, the Tablet of Beth'Amara. I was wondering if my partnership with Jediga had failed or if the poor orc had found her death in Azshara. I am glad she was successful.\nBeth'Amara was one of the Highborne's most influential alchemists. The wizard alone was said to have mastered transmuting metals among other things.\nAzshara Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":22.6,"y":51.4,"n":"Jediga","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":69.9,"y":30.9,"n":"Magatha Grimtotem","e":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"718":{"id":718,"t":"Mirages","lv":38,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Supply Crate for Sigrun Ironhew.\nSupply Crate Excavation Supply Crate","desc":"In our hurry to leave the Uldaman excavation site, we were forced to abandon many wagons and crates of supplies along the way. The local ogres from Camp Kosh have been on our abandoned equipment like vultures on a rotting corpse. Don't smell much better, either. Than the corpses, I mean.\nAnyways, they took the cart that was carrying all our weapons and such... so--well, this is a bit embarrassing--we haven't been able to get any food.\nWe're in a bit of a pickle here, suppose you could help us out?","rew":"Experience: 2,150\n+75 reputation with Ironforge","back":"The desert's a bad place to be hungry, my friend, let me tell you that.\nHey... what's that over there...","done":"Thanks so much, ‹name›. While you were gone, I... er... swallowed a mouthful of sand. It...\nWell, enough of that, we'll go out and get some food tonight. Eat like kings!","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":53.8,"y":43.3,"n":"Sigrun Ironhew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"1198":{"id":1198,"t":"In Search of Thaelrid","lv":24,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,700 experience instead of 2,400, 2.38 times as much. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Seek out Argent Guard Thaelrid in Blackfathom Deeps.","desc":"Many rumors circulate these days about the union of the Twilight's Hammer and the naga in Blackfathom Deeps on the coasts of Ashenvale.\nMy role here with the Argent Dawn is to collect as much information as I can, so we know when and where help is needed.\nIt has been weeks now since I sent a scout to check on the activity at Blackfathom Deeps. Argent Guard Thaelrid has not yet reported back.\nMy other scouts are preoccupied with pressing matters.\nSeek out and aid Thaelrid for me, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 5,700\n+150 reputation with Argent Dawn\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Dawnwatcher Shaedlass was good to send you. There is indeed a wicked plot underway in this corrupted place.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":55.4,"y":25,"n":"Dawnwatcher Shaedlass","s":1}],"cats":["blackfathom-deeps"]},"97918":{"id":97918,"t":"Camping 101 engineering","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Sprite Jumpsprocket in Stormwind to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your engineering skill to 20","desc":"Engineers like yourself can cook up all sorts of bits, bots, and bombs for fun and profit.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a Reagent Bot for your camp. This helpful automaton can help keep you well-supplied so that you and your allies never run out of the materials needed to fuel your spells.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Reagent Bot. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nElwynn Forest Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":44.8,"y":63.2,"n":"Sam Sarsaparilla","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":54.6,"y":8,"n":"Sprite Jumpsprocket","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96638":{"id":96638,"t":"The adventurer","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to Raan Wildwind near Shen'dar Village.","desc":"More and more adventurers like yourself have been seeking glory and fortune outside of the safety of Thendal Grove. There's one such adventurer who has made a camp outside of Shen'dar Village, along the road leading southwest out of Thendal Grove.\nSeek him out and see what you can learn from him that may help you in your own travels.","done":"Well met!","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42.6,"y":23.6,"n":"Aetheen of the Gales","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":41.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Raan Wildwind","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"95998":{"id":95998,"t":"The great outdoors","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Sit near Sam's Basic Campfire by typing /sit in the chat window and wait until you receive the Boosted Rest buff.\nUse the /sit emote near the campfire\nGain the Boosted Rest buff","desc":"Well howdy there, ‹class›. I can see you've got the look of an adventurer about you. Good for you. The world needs more of us restless souls, seeking fortune and glory.\nIt's a big wide world out there and you'll need to learn to thrive in the wilds to be successful. Not sure how your outdoorsman skills are but I reckon I could teach you a thing or two, if you'd be apt to learn.\nHave a seat near the fire, get comfy. I'll walk you through it.","back":"Having the skills needed to survive the outdoors are critical. A well-rested and well-prepared adventurer has a much higher chance of surviving this lifestyle.","done":"So now that we've learned the basics, why don't you go and learn a tradeskill. They will also teach you the know-how to create a proper camp fixture suitable to your new profession.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":44.8,"y":63.2,"n":"Sam Sarsaparilla","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94318":{"id":94318,"t":"Craftsmans writ greater fire protection potion","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Greater Fire Protection Potion\nGreater Fire Protection Potion","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Greater Fire Protection Potion, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Greater Fire Protection Potion Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94318","cats":["crafting"]},"94238":{"id":94238,"t":"Craftsmans writ heavy leather ball","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Heavy Leather Ball\nHeavy Leather Ball","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Heavy Leather Ball, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Heavy Leather Ball Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94238","cats":["crafting"]},"958":{"id":958,"t":"Tools of the Highborne","lv":12,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve 7 Highborne Relics for Thundris Windweaver in Auberdine.\n7 Highborne Relic Wailing Highborne 40 % , Writhing Highborne 40 % , Cursed Highborne 40 %","desc":"‹class›. A task I would ask of you.\nHave you seen the ruins of Ameth'Aran? If not, you will find them on the eastern side of the main road, some ways to the south. Once they were the home of many powerful Highborne, now they are a testament to the destruction their dabblings produced.\nI have been told by the Sentinels that the spirits of the Highborne persist, and that they wield their ancient magical implements. Those relics must be appropriated, so that we might destroy them.","rew":"You will receive:\nIvy Cuffs\nMoney: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 900\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"If only the tools of their undoing could have been destroyed in the cataclysm that destroyed our world... Nonetheless, we must do what we can to ensure that the horrors of our past are not repeated in the future.","done":"Though it is surely a figment of my imagination, I feel as though I can almost feel the taint of foul Highborne magic upon them. I will have these destroyed, so that their long dormant evil might never be released again.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":37.4,"y":40.1,"n":"Thundris Windweaver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"2078":{"id":2078,"t":"Gyromast's Revenge","lv":20,"min":14,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Gelkak's First Mate, the Threshwackonator 4100, and lead it back to Gelkak.\nGelkak's First Mate\nProvided: Gyromast's Key","desc":"Landlubber, ye needs to find me first mate.\nTake this'n key, puts it in his gulliver an' bring him back here to serve the Cap'n.\nThem murlocs an' their chief ain't gonna be too happy once me first mate gets a hold of em!","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Draught of Water Breathing\nMoney: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Where be me first mate, ‹name›? Shackles n' sharks fer ye soon if ye don't hurry!","done":"Yarrr... Ye be provin' yerself to be more than a yella sea dog, landlubber.\nThe Cap'n may promote ye to poop deck swabby if ye be keepin' this up...","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":56.7,"y":13.5,"n":"Gelkak Gyromast","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"1438":{"id":1438,"t":"Vahlarriel's Search","lv":33,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Dalinda Malem in Desolace.","desc":"Find both Dalinda and Tyranis if you can and come back to me with your findings. Start your search at this fortress. I will contact my superiors in Darnassus immediately and let them know the situation.\n‹name›, there is something else I wish to impress upon you. My superiors have shown some concern over Tyranis' and his motives for coming here. It is more important to them that Dalinda is found and brought back safely. Tyranis is to be... gauged before he is taken home.","rew":"Experience: 2,650\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Thank Elune someone has finally come to help. Please, ‹class›, I need your help. My brother Tyranis and I were captured and brought here by the Burning Blade. I think they mean to sacrifice me to their demon masters!\nI knew coming to Desolace was a mistake, but Tyranis has recently begun craving knowledge of all things arcane--even against the wishes of our people. He decided to make this trek even after hearing tales of this land's demon infestation.\nI fear the worst for him.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":66.4,"y":11.8,"n":"Vahlarriel Demonslayer","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":54.9,"y":26.1,"n":"Dalinda Malem","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"5518":{"id":5518,"t":"The Gordok Ogre Suit","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 4 Bolts of Runecloth, 8 Rugged Leather, 2 Rune Threads, and Ogre Tannin to Knot Thimblejack. He is currently chained inside the Gordok wing of Dire Maul.\n4 Bolt of Runecloth Felsteel Chest 0.9 % , Twilight Lord Everun 0 %\n8 Rugged Leather sold by Lhara\n2 Rune Thread sold by Banalash , sold by Nerrist , sold by Edna Mullby , sold by Alexandra Bolero and 4 more\nOgre Tannin Doomguard Minion , Ogre Tannin Basket , Knot Thimblejack's Cache 35 % , Gordok Warlock 0.8 % and 3 more","desc":"If you're going to fight the king of this dump - and I think that's what you're bound to do - then you're going to need to get by Captain Kromcrush. Now, you can get by him by killing him, sure. You might actually want to leave him alive.\nHow, you ask? Since I've been here, I think I know how to make an ogre suit that will last just long enough to fool these bozos. The only problem is stability - ten minutes tops. Bring me what I need, and I'll make you one. I'm not going anywhere...","rew":"You will receive:\nGordok Ogre Suit\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","back":"The Ogre Tannin is probably the toughest thing to find for what I need to make the suit - I think they have some upstairs? It's hard to tell, since this ball and chain doesn't make movement that easy to do...\nAnyway, bring me the things I need, and I'll whip you up an ogre suit that will fool Captain Kromcrush into thinking you're one of his men.","done":"Yeah, this will do the trick. Just a slip here, and tuck here... heh - this is going to work out just fine! <A broad smile beams from the chained goblin's face.>\nHere you go, you're all set. Remember- this isn't the most securely fashioned item in the world. You'll have ten minutes of use before it falls apart, and then you're not going to fool anybody! Try using it just before you approach him, and remember... it only will make him think that YOU are an ally - not your group mates!\nStart Knot Thimblejack End Knot Thimblejack Level 60 , requires level 56 Difficulty 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 5518\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 6,600 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] The Gordok Ogre Suit this quest\nBring 4 Bolts of Runecloth, 8 Rugged Leather, 2 Rune Threads, and Ogre Tannin to Knot Thimblejack.\nKnot Thimblejack\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] The Gordok Ogre Suit\nKnot Thimblejack","cats":["dire-maul"]},"94638":{"id":94638,"t":"Strength and mercy","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find and kill Ur'endra in the Shen'dar Highlands.\nUr'endra slain","desc":"You have come to me in hopes of learning to take a shape of strength. I have a task for you, though it lays heavy on my heart.\nMy mate, Ur'endra, has lost herself to madness and has begun to attack her own kin. Without the winds many creatures have begun to lose themselves, and with Ur'endra's great might she poses a dire threat to the delicate balance. She roams the Shen'dar Highlands to the northwest of here.\nShow me you have the fortitude to end her suffering and I shall grant you my blessing.","done":"The agony I feel over her loss is immeasurable, but it is what is necessary for the balance. You have demonstrated a resolve to persevere, even when a terrible price is asked.\nYou have done well, ‹class›. I shall grant you the blessing to take on the shape of my kin. Be a beacon for those that lack the strength to persevere and a defender of those in need.\nGo now, and embrace the way of the claw, child.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":69.8,"y":61.6,"n":"Urs'endris","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"318":{"id":318,"t":"Evershine","lv":7,"min":2,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get a cask of Evershine from Rejold Barleybrew in Brewnall Village.","desc":"Rejold Barleybrew experiments with his brews. Some of them taste good, some bad, and some...well, some will lay all but the stoutest dwarf flat.\nHe lives at Brewnall Village, west of Kharanos, and one of his drinks, Evershine, is what I want. It'll help keep me warm while I'm on the cold road.\nAnd...the blessed stuff burns so hot I can throw it in Jetsteam's furnace for a burst of power! That little tactic has gotten me out of more than one tight spot.","rew":"Experience: 160\n+25 reputation with Ironforge\n+25 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","done":"Bellowfiz needs some of my Evershine? Hm...all right.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":49.4,"y":48.4,"n":"Pilot Bellowfiz","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":30.2,"y":45.7,"n":"Rejold Barleybrew","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"158":{"id":158,"t":"Zombie Juice","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Tavernkeep Smitts.","desc":"I need a bottle of a certain liquor - Zombie Juice. Tavernkeep Smitts at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire should have some.\nAnd please hurry, ‹name›. These nights get cold, and I need that drink to put fire in my veins again!","rew":"Experience: 490","done":"You need some Zombie Juice, do you? Hmm...that's some strong stuff - I don't usually get requests for it.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":28.1,"y":31.5,"n":"Abercrombie","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.8,"y":44.5,"n":"Tavernkeep Smitts","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"78":{"id":78,"t":"The Legend of Stalvan","lv":28,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Faded Journal Page to Tavernkeep Smitts.\nA Faded Journal Page Marshal Haggard's Chest\nProvided: A Faded Journal Page","desc":"I know of someone who might be able to assist you. Back when I was leading the Stormwind Guard, we used to get drinks at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire. The Innkeeper there, Smitts, was quite an expert on the local lore. Show him this page and see what he has to say about it.","rew":"Experience: 575\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Marshal Haggard sent you? Why didn't you say so?\nAh, good ol' Haggard. Poor chap is going to be completely blind before long. Anyway, let me see what you've got there.","done":"By the Light! You bet I recognize that handwriting.\nElwynn Forest Duskwood","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":84.6,"y":69.4,"n":"Marshal Haggard","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.8,"y":44.5,"n":"Tavernkeep Smitts","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"9198":{"id":9198,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Thorium Tube","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 14 Thorium Tubes and the Craftsman's Writ - Thorium Tube - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Thorium Tube\n14 Thorium Tube\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Thorium Tube","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order EN-558:\n14 Thorium Tubes.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"Thorium tubes? Gee, thanks.\n<Packmaster Stonebruiser throws the stack of thorium tubes into a large pile of assorted junk.>","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"7678":{"id":7678,"t":"Palomino Exchange","lv":1,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Palomino Bridle","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSwift Brown Steed Swift Palomino Swift White Steed","back":"[PH] If you bring me your palomino, I'll trade it in for one from the new herd. The new horse will be just as fast as your old one, but have a different look to it. You can look at the swift steeds here to see what it will look like.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":84.2,"y":65.5,"n":"Katie Hunter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"91758":{"id":91758,"t":"Follow that kobold","lv":4,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to Tordrin Sternblade near the stable behind Northshire's Abbey.","desc":"You're not done with those kobolds yet. We just got word from Kelsey that a kobold left the mine carrying a large sack of books. I need you to track down this kobold so we can retrieve the books for Brother Paxton.\nGo talk to Tordrin Sternblade. He's the new Hunter trainer that just arrived from Ironforge. You can find him behind the abbey, near the stable. He can help you track this kobold thief.","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 0 silver, 35 copper Experience: 180\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","done":"I can help ye' track down this varmint. Let me whip somethin' up for ye'.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":48.8,"y":41.6,"n":"Marshal McBride","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":51.2,"y":40.8,"n":"Tordrin Sternblade","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"2158":{"id":2158,"t":"Rest and Relaxation","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 110 experience instead of 100, 1.1 times as much.","obj":"Speak with Innkeeper Farley at the Lion's Pride Inn.","desc":"Every adventurer should rest when exhaustion sets in - and there is no finer place to get rest and relaxation than at the Lion's Pride Inn!\nMy best friend, Innkeeper Farley, runs the Lion's Pride. If you tell him I sent you, he may give you the special discounted rates on food and drink.\nTo find the Lion's Pride Inn, travel south along the road from here -- you can't miss it!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n5 Small Pumpkin 5 Refreshing Spring Water\nExperience: 110\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Rest and relaxation for the tired and cold -- that's our motto! Please, take a seat by the fire and rest your weary bones.\nWould you like to try a sampling of some of our fine food and drink?","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":45.6,"y":47.7,"n":"Falkhaan Isenstrider","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.8,"y":65.8,"n":"Innkeeper Farley","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"2878":{"id":2878,"t":"Corrupted Songflower","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a songflower plant. A pungent, unhealthy odor emanates from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply some Cenarion plant salve to the songflower. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":63.3,"y":22.6,"n":"Corrupted Songflower","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"8958":{"id":8958,"t":"Anthion's Parting Words","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Deliana in Ironforge with a set of Dreadmist Sandals, Dreadmist Leggings and Dreadmist Mantle.\nDreadmist Sandals Baroness Anastari 0 % in Stratholme\nDreadmist Leggings Baron Rivendare 0 % in Stratholme\nDreadmist Mantle Jandice Barov 17 % in Scholomance\nProvided: Top Piece of Lord Valthalak's Amulet","desc":"Valthalak's soul was stored in this amulet. In our greed we foolishly split it into three parts, not knowing the curse that would await us.\nThe only way to stop Valthalak's spell is to put the medallion back together. Return to Deliana and tell her that Bodley is her only hope for finding the remaining pieces. Speak to her about any rewards you've arranged for.\nI, for once, shall rest in peace. I wish you the best of luck; you shall need every bit of it!","rew":"You will receive:\nDeathmist Sandals Deathmist Leggings Deathmist Mantle\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're back, ‹name›. You must tell me all about what you've found out. But first let us arrange for your reward.","done":"I can't believe our lives are all but forfeit all because of a stupid medallion! And you're sure Anthion mentioned Bodley?\nWell, you've done your job so let's get your reward out of the way.\nEastern Plaguelands Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8718":{"id":8718,"t":"Bladeswift the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The heavens, in their countless stars, hold answers to earthly mysteries, ‹name›. Might, then, the wise, and the lucky, gaze up and find truth?","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":33.5,"y":14.3,"n":"Elder Bladeswift","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8878":{"id":8878,"t":"Festive Recipes","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"5 Coin of Ancestry","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nPattern: Festival Dress Pattern: Festival Suit\nYou will also receive:\nLunar Festival Fireworks Pack","back":"The dresses and pant suits you see are traditional clothes from many years past.\nThey are worn in honor of old ways and loved ones gone. If you bring me coins of ancestry, <name>, then I will give you the pattern to create traditional red dresses or suits.","done":"Here are the patterns, ‹name›. I am sure you will find the product of this knowledge quite beautiful.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":53.8,"y":35.3,"n":"Fariel Starsong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9118":{"id":9118,"t":"Bindings of Faith","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Father Inigo Montoy at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Bindings of Faith if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Bindings, 6 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 1 Arcane Crystal and 1 Nexus Crystal.\nDesecrated Bindings Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Grand Widow Faerlina 0 % in Naxxramas , Anub'Rekhan 0 % in Naxxramas\n6 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcane Crystal Hakkari Thorium Vein 5.8 % , Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Ooze Covered Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Small Thorium Vein 2.6 % and 4 more\nNexus Crystal","desc":"<Father Montoy makes some strange gestures in the air in front of you.>\nBlessed boy/girl, have you found the vestments of the fallen? The poor souls whose last breaths were taken on the field of battle - stripped of everything including their dignity.\nBring me the desecrated remnants of the departed along with reagents of purification and you shall know faith.","rew":"You will receive:\nBindings of Faith\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Bindings of Faith.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Father Inigo Montoy","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9038":{"id":9038,"t":"Dreadnaught Pauldrons","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Korfax at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Dreadnaught Pauldrons if you bring him the following items: 1 Desecrated Pauldrons, 12 Wartorn Plate Scraps, 2 Arcanite Bars and 3 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Pauldrons Grobbulus 0 % in Naxxramas , Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Patchwerk 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Plate Scrap Infectious Ghoul 22.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 21.6 % in Naxxramas , Plagued Deathhound 21.3 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 20.8 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n2 Arcanite Bar\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"During your battles with the Scourge in Naxxramas, should you come across desecrated battlements and wartorn plate scraps, return them to me and I shall craft for you a piece of armor worn by heroes.","rew":"You will receive:\nDreadnaught Pauldrons\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Dreadnaught Pauldrons.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":72,"y":48.5,"n":"Korfax, Champion of the Light","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"5678":{"id":5678,"t":"Arcane feedback","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Laurena in Stormwind.","desc":"It is time for you to return to Stormwind, young one. Your superiors there have called you back for more training. And although it disturbs me some, your race and mine are allies and I would not betray that.\nI do not mean to be so coy with you--my distrust of arcane magics, be they divine inspired or not, is still strong within me.\nYou will know of what I speak after you return to your Cathedral of Light. Speak to High Priestess Laurena when you arrive.","done":"Ah, you have wonderful timing, ‹name›. I was beginning to wonder if all of my messengers had been successful. I'm glad to see they were, otherwise I would wager you'd still be out in the world learning more about all the threats that exist against our people.\nAre you ready? Ready for more training I mean. You're growing in power more quickly, and I feel you are ready to learn more about our faith.\nDarnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":39.2,"y":81,"n":"Priestess Alathea","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":38.8,"y":26.4,"n":"High Priestess Laurena","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"3118":{"id":3118,"t":"Encrypted Sigil","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Encrypted Sigil and speak to Frahun Shadewhisper in Shadowglen.\nEncrypted Sigil\nProvided: Encrypted Sigil","desc":"This sigil was given to me by a messenger from our rogue trainer, Frahun. It seems Frahun would have words with you when you have a moment. Read it and bring it to him afterwards.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Hello, Ferlis. I'm glad you found me. I was thinking that perhaps you got lost on the way here.\nNothing really new has happened in Shadowglen since I sent you my sigil, but I'll leave all the information gathering to you. Speak to the rest of the people around Aldrassil if you'd like.","done":"Until then, know that our kind are needed more than ever in this tenuous time. Peace with the other races can fail at any moment, and there is much talk about members of the Horde looking to sow even greater seeds of distrust. Remember that.\nAs you gain in power and feel more prepared, come back to me here and I will see about getting you some training. It's important that you know how to handle your weapon of choice, among other things.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":58.7,"y":44.3,"n":"Conservator Ilthalaine","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":59.6,"y":38.7,"n":"Frahun Shadewhisper","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"2238":{"id":2238,"t":"Simple Subterfugin'","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Onin MacHammar by Gnomeregan.","desc":"Ye see, the King be strip mining the quarry fer ore and gems. More riches than any one dwarf should see in ten lifetimes.\nThe Hidden Circle has values, ‹name›. We value valuables. Can ye understand?\nNow we feels the King should be sharing some of that booty, but we don't want ol' 'Stinkbeard' to know he's sharin' - if ye catch me drift.\nWe needs ye to speak with Onin MacHammar over by Gnomeregan and bring back a report. The crafty dwarf has hidden hisself amongst the lepers. Be careful.","rew":"Experience: 850","done":"Shhhh! Keep it down you daft fool. They'll hear us.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.4,"y":23.5,"n":"Hulfdan Blackbeard","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":25.2,"y":44.5,"n":"Onin MacHammar","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"1998":{"id":1998,"t":"Fenwick Thatros","lv":16,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill Fenwick Thatros and bring his head back to Mennet Carkad in the Rogues' Quarter of the Undercity.\nFenwick's Head Fenwick Thatros","desc":"Lord Varimathras has just sent me a missive about a threat to the Forsaken that must be immediately removed. His name is Fenwick Thatros, one whom Lord Varimathras believes is a leader of the undead that have taken root in Silverpine Forest.\nYour name came to mind immediately, ‹name›. I have faith enough in your abilities that you will carry out this mission flawlessly.\nThe latest reports from the Deathstalkers in Silverpine indicate that Thatros can be found near the decrepit dock on Lordamere.","rew":"Experience: 875","back":"I have placed the utmost faith in you to perform this service for Lord Varimathras.","done":"You've done well, ‹name›. It occurs to me that you have performed many services for the Deathstalkers, proving your worth, and that perhaps it is time that we furthered your training in the shadow arts.\nUndercity Silverpine Forest","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":83.5,"y":69.1,"n":"Mennet Carkad","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"2478":{"id":2478,"t":"Mission: Possible But Not Probable","lv":24,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Steal Silixiz's Tower Key from Foreman Silixiz, then kill two Mutated Venture Co. Drones, two Venture Co. Patrollers, and two Venture Co. Lookouts.\nAssassinate Grand Foreman Gallywix and take his head, then pick the lock on Gallywix's lockbox and steal the Cache of Zanzil's Altered Mixture. Take the Cache and Gallywix's Head back to Shenthul in Orgrimmar for further instruction.\nGallywix's Head Grand Foreman Puzik Gallywix\nSilixiz's Tower Key\nCache of Zanzil's Altered Mixture Gallywix's Lockbox\nMutated Venture Co. Drone slain : 0/ 2\nVenture Co. Lookout slain : 0/ 2\nVenture Co. Patroller slain : 0/ 2","desc":"You will need to steal the tower key from Foreman Silixiz, ‹name›. Once you've got the key in your possession, hold on to it - I may need it later.\nRemember, the poison has weakened everything in this tower. Use your abilities to bring chaos and destruction to its inhabitants. Slay them all -- show no mercy!\nOnce everything inside lays in a bloodied heap, pick Gallywix's lockbox and steal the cache of Zanzil's mixture held inside. Take both the head of Gallywix and the mixture to Shenthul in Orgrimmar.","rew":"You will receive:\nRecipe: Thistle Tea\nExperience: 1,950","back":"What have you to report, ‹name›?","done":"Poor Fizzule, he was a good agent -- one of our best. Alas, it is the price we pay, ‹name›. Being a field agent of the Shattered Hand is dangerous work.\nYou have performed your duty well, ‹class›. It would be a shame if you did not live to serve us again.\nThe Barrens Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":55.4,"y":5.6,"n":"Taskmaster Fizzule","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":43,"y":53.7,"n":"Shenthul","e":1}],"cats":["rogue"]},"1518":{"id":1518,"t":"Call of Earth","lv":4,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Rough Quartz to Canaga Earthcaller in the Valley of Trials.\nRough Quartz\nProvided: Rough Quartz","desc":"Take this rough quartz from me and bring it to Canaga Earthcaller as proof of our meeting. He will craft a totem for you, and this pebble will be the heart of it. As small as it may seem, you will come to find that size does not matter, and that even the smallest of things can outlast many others.\nBe patient, ‹name›. Remain strong. And seek wisdom. This is what earth asks of you. In the end, you shall become one with the earth--respect it as it shall respect you.","rew":"You will receive:\nEarth Totem\nYou will learn: Stoneskin Totem\nExperience: 450","back":"I wish to be the first to welcome you fully to the first of four paths that will forever lead you in your destiny.\nIf you have the stone the earth gave to you, I will give you the totem it promised.\nIf not, then be gone with you until you have found your way.","done":"Excellent!\nThe totem I will craft for you is more than a symbol of your status among ‹class›--it has abilities beyond that. One use of the totem is as a focus for spells. Those spells are tied to the earth, and as you earn greater and greater wisdom, more of the earth's abilities will be made accessible to you.\nThe trainers will know when you are ready for greater knowledge.\nBut for now, take this earth totem, and a scroll to teach you your first ability.\nDurotar Mulgore","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":44,"y":76.2,"n":"Minor Manifestation of Earth","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":42.4,"y":69.2,"n":"Canaga Earthcaller","e":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":52,"y":80.4,"n":"Minor Manifestation of Earth","s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"79358":{"id":79358,"t":"Storm earth and fire","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 5 Twisted Fire Totems, 5 Twisted Earth Totems, 5 Twisted Air Totems, and 5 Twisted Water Totems for Veyric Thunderhame in Arathi Highlands.\n5 Twisted Water Totem\n5 Twisted Earth Totem\n5 Twisted Fire Totem\n5 Twisted Air Totem","desc":"Floodin' the Thousand Needles is no small feat, ‹name›. If I hadn't felt the elements' outrage meself, I'd have never believed it. But here we are.\nThe quilboar aren't the first tae weaponize the elements irresponsibly, and they won't be the last. If we want to prepare our own counter-ritual, we'll need a better understanding of these twisted elements. Take this book. It details the many denizens of Azeroth and how they practice shamanism.\nIf you can learn from them, maybe we can find a solution.","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,850","back":"What've ye brought me?\nArathi Highlands Badlands","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":59.8,"y":27.6,"n":"Veyric Thunderhame","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8318":{"id":8318,"t":"Secret Communication","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Encrypted Twilight Texts to Bor Wildmane in Cenarion Hold.\n10 Encrypted Twilight Text Twilight Prophet , Twilight Marauder 25 % , Twilight Marauder Morna 25 % , Twilight Overlord 25 % and 4 more","desc":"Some of the Twilight's Hammer cultists carry around little papers with gibberish written on them. I want you to bring me a stack of them, ‹class›.\nI can't figure out what the gibberish means, but that's not the point! These papers are how their different groups communicate secretly. The more texts we take out of circulation, the less they can communicate!","rew":"Money: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me some texts?","done":"Excellent! I'll stash these away, maybe they'll be useful later.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":48.6,"y":37.8,"n":"Bor Wildmane","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"478":{"id":478,"t":"Maps and Runes","lv":14,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the strange pendant to Shadow Priest Allister at the Sepulcher.\nRune-inscribed Pendant\nProvided: Rune-inscribed Pendant","desc":"<You quickly remove the pendant from the crate and replace the lid.>","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 750\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"Have you learned anything useful, ‹name›?","done":"Maps and this... pendant, hm? Interesting.\nIt is obvious that the Dalaran wizards are interested in Ambermill for some purpose, but still, their aim is hidden to me.\nPerhaps Dalar will know something of their use.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":49.9,"y":60.3,"n":"Dalaran Crate","s":1},{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44,"y":40.9,"n":"Shadow Priest Allister","e":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"84398":{"id":84398,"t":"A study of the light","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"A Study of the Light","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nA Study of the Light (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":38.6,"y":79.4,"n":"Jennea Cannon","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.4,"y":32.4,"n":"Oran Snakewrithe","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"558":{"id":558,"t":"Jaina's Autograph","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Theramore to see about getting Lady Jaina Proudmoore's autograph for your ward.\nJaina's Autograph","desc":"They say that Lady Jaina Proudmoore in Theramore is one of the greatest heroes the Alliance has ever had. When I grow up, I wanna be a hero of the Alliance too!\nDo you know Jaina, ‹name›? Could you do me a favor, please? Could you get her autograph for me? I dunno how to ask her, and she'd probably be too busy for someone like me... but you! You're an adventurer just like she is! I bet she'd give you her autograph easy!\nPlease?","rew":"Experience: 650\n+75 reputation with Alliance","back":"Someday, I wanna be a hero just like Jaina... well, a boy hero that is.","done":"WOW! You got Lady Jaina's autograph for me! Thank you very much! And wow... she wrote a personal message on here - to me! I knew she'd be totally cool, and maybe someday I'll thank her myself... when I become a hero of the Alliance!\nYou're the best, ‹name›. Thank you for being so nice to me.\nStart Human Orphan End Human Orphan Level 60 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 56 58 Side Both factions Shareable No Quest ID 558\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 2,300 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Jaina's Autograph this quest\nTravel to Theramore to see about getting Lady Jaina Proudmoore's autograph for your ward.\nHuman Orphan\n650 XP\n2 [ 60 ] A Warden of the Alliance\nReturn your ward to the Stormwind orphanage by handing in the Human Orphan Whistle to Orphan Matron Nightingale in the Cathedral District.\nHuman Orphan\n1,650 XP","cats":["special"]},"638":{"id":638,"t":"Trollbane","lv":37,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Hammerfall in the Arathi Highlands and speak with Zengu.","desc":"With Thoras Trollbane dead and Stromgarde in ruins, Vol'jin has instructed that we make every effort to spirit the legendary sword Trol'kalar from the humans' hands, so that we might use it in our coming battles against the trolls of Zul'Gurub.\nZengu, one of our seasoned hunters, was dispatched to Hammerfall in northeastern Arathi Highlands to oversee its procurement.","rew":"Experience: 700\n+25 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","done":"How you doing, ‹class›? The task set before us by Vol'jin will be a difficult one, and any assistance you might provide will be appreciated and necessary.\nStranglethorn Vale Arathi Highlands","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.2,"y":27.7,"n":"Nimboya","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.8,"y":34,"n":"Zengu","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"7838":{"id":7838,"t":"Arena Grandmaster","lv":55,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"12 Arena Master Arena Treasure Chest","desc":"Avast Lubber! Bring me 12 trinkets of the Arena Master and then ye shall be a Grandmaster of the Gurubashi Arena! Arrrr!","rew":"You will receive:\nArena Grand Master","back":"Avast Lubber! Bring me 12 trinkets of the Arena Master.","done":"Much blood have you spilt on the Arena floor and I be glad to name you Grandmaster of the Arena!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":29.6,"y":47.4,"n":"Short John Mithril","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8238":{"id":8238,"t":"Gurubashi, Vilebranch, and Witherbark Coins","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gurubashi Coin Hakkari Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadowcaster 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadow Hunter 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Blood Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more\nVilebranch Coin Hakkari Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadowcaster 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadow Hunter 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Blood Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more\nWitherbark Coin Hakkari Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadowcaster 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Shadow Hunter 5 % in Zul'Gurub , Hakkari Blood Priest 5 % in Zul'Gurub and 4 more","desc":"I seek the Paragons of Power known as the Coins of the Tribes. They are the currency used by the various denizens of Zul'Gurub, and each is imbued with subtle but powerful mojo.\nThere are nine distinct kinds to be found. Some are sought after by my compatriots for various armors they offer Zandalar heroes. Should you have any extra, I will trade you one of our Honor Tokens for a set of three. You may use the Tokens with Rin'wosho the Trader; he offers our heroes special items for them.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Honor Token\nExperience: 650\n+25 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"I seek the Paragons of Power known as the Coins of the Tribes. They are the currency used by the various denizens of Zul'Gurub, and each is imbued with subtle but powerful mojo.\nThere are nine distinct kinds to be found. Should you have any extra, I will trade you one of our Honor Tokens for a set of three. You may use the Tokens with Rin'wosho the Trader; he offers our heroes special items for them.","done":"Excellent - this set of coins will make a fine addition to our growing collection... one that we will use in the tribe's defense against the rise of the Blood God. You've earned this Honor Token, ‹name›, as well as the thanks of the tribe!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.5,"y":15.8,"n":"Vinchaxa","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8078":{"id":8078,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Vindicator's Belt","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Bring Jin'rokh the Breaker a Primal Hakkari Girdle. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Honored with the Zandalar Tribe.\nJin'rokh the Breaker is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Girdle\nReach 9000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"The ultimate vengeance waits within Zul'Gurub. Hakkar must not rise again. Hakkar destroyed the Gurubashi Empire from within. No sacrifice was enough. The trolls are a shadow of former glories. I know this is because of Hakkar.\nBecome the vindicator you were meant to be. Wreak havoc on the minions of evil. Zul'Gurub must taste Zandalar vengeance. Bring me proof in the Paragons of Power. You will receive the vindicator's belt. You will receive real power.\nGo.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Vindicator's Belt\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Have you brought the Paragons of Power? Have you struck down the enemies of the tribe? Hakkar must know the wrath of the vindicator!","done":"The way of the vindicator is now known to you. You have brought honor to the tribe. You have brought honor to yourself. You have brought pain to our enemies.\nThe vindicator's belt is yours. You are surely becoming one with the way of the vindicator.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":14.4,"n":"Jin'rokh the Breaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"98398":{"id":98398,"t":"The oracle tree","lv":12,"min":6,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Find the Oracle Tree Bark nearby to receive its message.","desc":"I am impressed by what you have accomplished here in so short a time, ‹name›. Would that I could ask you to remain here to assist me with my duties... but I know in my heart that greater tasks lie ahead for you.\nI have noticed the Oracle Tree has just shed a piece of its bark. No doubt it has a task that it wishes completed. You should speak with it.","done":"As you inspect the fallen bark, a voice enters your mind. It is calm and soothing, cresting over you like a gentle breeze through the leaves.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":38.2,"y":34.4,"n":"Sentinel Arynia Cloudsbreak","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":37,"y":34.1,"n":"Oracle Tree Bark","e":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"878":{"id":878,"t":"Tribes at War","lv":21,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 6 Bristleback Water Seekers, 12 Bristleback Thornweavers and 12 Bristleback Geomancers and return to Mangletooth at Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.\nBristleback Water Seeker slain : 0/ 6\nBristleback Thornweaver slain : 0/ 12\nBristleback Geomancer slain : 0/ 12","desc":"You must strike my enemies. <snort> You must help Mangletooth and the Razormane by weakening the Bristlebacks. Both tribes are very spiritual--tied to the earth and its power. <snort> It gives us strength in all things... especially war.\nIf you want to find out who really causes Thork <snort> and the Horde such anguish, then help Mangletooth! You attack the spiritual leaders of the Bristlebacks to the north; weaken them so the Razormanes can defeat them and rule the Barrens.","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"More information <snort> for the Horde when you've killed the Bristleback's wise ones, ‹race›. <snort> Not a moment earlier! Mangletooth is no fool.","done":"Yes, yes... filled with joy because finally <snort> the Bristleback know my tribe's pain, ‹race›. That is how I should feel, but that <snort> is not the case.\nYou aid your people and they honor you. Mangletooth aids his people, and what do they do? They turn their backs on him. They forget him and leave him to rot in cage!\nI aid them even from locked behind bars and they send no one to save me!","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.5,"y":59.3,"n":"Mangletooth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"1118":{"id":1118,"t":"Back to Booty Bay","lv":43,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Kravel's Scheme to Crank Fizzlebub in Booty Bay.\nKravel's Scheme\nProvided: Kravel's Scheme","desc":"‹name›, you're a ‹class› I can trust, both to get the job done and to keep your mouth shut while doing it.\nI've been brewing up a new scheme. It's risky, but if it works then we could both make a bundle! And I think you're just the person to see it through.\nTo start, you must go back to Booty Bay. I apologize, good ‹name›. I know my last task took you there. But this time, speak with Crank Fizzlebub.\nGive him this letter. And if he requires aid, do your best to help him. It will be worth the effort.","rew":"Experience: 900","back":"Hello hello. And what brings a noble ‹race› such as you down to Booty Bay?","done":"I see. Kravel has a big scheme planned. He has a sinister mind -- I like that about him.\nSo you'll need something to addle wits, eh? Something powerful...\nI wonder if the mixture Zanzil feeds his zombies could be used...\nThousand Needles Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":77.8,"y":77.3,"n":"Kravel Koalbeard","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.1,"y":77.2,"n":"Crank Fizzlebub","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"398":{"id":398,"t":"Wanted: Maggot Eye","lv":10,"min":6,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Wanted: Maggot Eye.","obj":"Kill Maggot Eye and return to Executor Zygand in Brill with his paw for a reward.\nMaggot Eye's Paw Maggot Eye","desc":"Wanted: Maggot Eye!\nA foul beast, even by Gnoll standards, Maggot Eye has been sentenced to death for his crimes against The Forsaken. This despicable villain has been stealing corpses for use by the Lich King's army. Maggot Eye was last seen pillaging the lands near Garren's Haunt to the north of Brill.\nThe town of Brill hereby offers a reward to the capable soul who can carry out the execution. Show Executor Zygand the villain's paw once the deed is done.\nMercy is for the weak.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBrass Scale Pants Tiller's Vest\nMoney: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Yes?","done":"Maggot Eye's dastardly acts have finally been avenged. Maybe your acts of valor will send a clear message to those who wish to bring harm to our people. On behalf of the town of Brill I thank you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":60.7,"y":51.5,"n":"Wanted!","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":60.6,"y":51.8,"n":"Executor Zygand","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"2398":{"id":2398,"t":"The Lost Dwarves","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 320 experience instead of 240, 1.33 times as much.","obj":"Find Baelog in Uldaman.","desc":"The dig site at Uldaman wasn't always overrun. We Ironforge dwarves used to control the area, but... that was before the troggs came. They came so fast and in such numbers that not even dwarven might could stop them!\nIn fact, their attack was so sudden that I fear some of our people may be trapped behind enemy lines.\nMy friend Baelog led a small band of dwarves deep within the site just before the troggs showed up. If he and his company live, then I want you to find them.","rew":"Money: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 320","done":"It's about time you showed up! I was in danger of losing a bet with Olaf!\nHe wagered that his beard would grow to his knees before he saw another living ‹race›. Well here you are, and as you can see Olaf's beard has a few more inches to go.\nThanks, ‹name›. I'll split the winnings with you.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.1,"y":23,"n":"Prospector Stormpike","s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"2318":{"id":2318,"t":"Translating the Journal","lv":42,"min":37,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 3,450 experience instead of 700, 4.93 times as much.","obj":"Find someone who can translate the paladin's journal. The closest location that might have someone is Kargath, in the Badlands.\nProvided: Untranslated Journal","desc":"At an impasse of sorts, you know that you will need the book translated into a language you can understand. There certainly are a number of people in the world who could do it; the closest location that might have someone who could, however, is the Kargath outpost in the Badlands. Perhaps that is a good place to start.","rew":"Experience: 3,450\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","done":"Mighty ‹class›, I know what you are doing out here in the Badlands. I know you seek my gift of tongues. You're after the parts to that necklace you found in Uldaman.\nSurprised? Don't be - it's my job to know such things. Instead, let's discuss what you're going to do for a translated journal. Trust me - I'm the only one you'll find that can translate it.\nBetter still, let me make you a better offer than Dran Droffers is, and it'll let you still complete your deal with them. Interested now, yes?","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":2.4,"y":46.1,"n":"Jarkal Mossmeld","e":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"1358":{"id":1358,"t":"Sample for Helbrim","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Wolf Heart Sample to Apothecary Helbrim in the Barrens.\nWolf Heart Sample\nProvided: Wolf Heart Sample","desc":"A colleague in Kalimdor, Apothecary Helbrim, is researching the effects of Lordaeron toxins on the beasts of Kalimdor. He would be very interested in a sample of the wolf hearts Renferrel sent me.\nHelbrim is stationed in the Barrens, in a village known as the Crossroads. To reach him, you must travel via zeppelin to the orc capital of Orgrimmar, then travel south, by foot, to Durotar. Head west into the Barrens, and you will soon reach the Crossroads.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBrewer's Gloves Long Draping Cape\nExperience: 1,050\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"You have a package for me?","done":"Ah, very good. If initial reports are true, then the toxicity of these hearts could lead to further advances in our knowledge of poisons.\nThis is a welcome delivery, ‹name›. Your reward is well earned.\nUndercity The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":50.1,"y":68,"n":"Apothecary Zinge","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.4,"y":30.2,"n":"Apothecary Helbrim","e":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"238":{"id":238,"t":"Errand for Apothecary Zinge","lv":45,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Field Sampling Kit to Apothecary Zinge in the Undercity.\nField Testing Kit sold by Alessandro Luca\nProvided: Field Testing Kit","desc":"The kit is ready, ‹name›. No doubt that Apothecary Zinge will want this as soon as possible. Take it to her without delay, and let her know that I will add the cost of the kit to the Society's tab. Also, please extend to her my warmest salutations.\nWell, don't just stand there. Such is the life of a simple courier, yes?","rew":"Experience: 390\n+10 reputation with Undercity","back":"Yes, I think Luca is as disturbing as you do. It matters not - hand me the field sampling kit. I will need to make some adjustments to it in order to survey for the proper base materials.\nYou have the kit, don't you?","done":"Good - it pleases me to be working with someone who takes pride in not wasting my time.\nAfter I make some adjustments to this kit, you'll be ready to head out into the field. You'll be using it to collect some vital data to the task at hand.\nIt will take just a moment for me to finish the modifications. While you are waiting, you should probably start thinking about what you'd like to bring to the desert with you.\nYes, I said the desert.\nUndercity Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":58.6,"y":54.7,"n":"Alessandro Luca","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":50.1,"y":68,"n":"Apothecary Zinge","e":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"1598":{"id":1598,"t":"The Stolen Tome","lv":4,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Powers of the Void for Drusilla La Salle.\nPowers of the Void Stolen Books","desc":"You there! ‹name›, right?\nI hope you're sure about becoming a warlock, because if you can't hold your own, you're likely to get pulled under.\nI'm to teach you, but I need to make sure you're strong enough first.\nThere was a novice studying at the Abbey who ran off to join the Defias Brotherhood. Why do I care? Well, he stole some important books.\nOne of those happens to be a book I've wanted for myself, the Powers of the Void. Steal it for me, they have it hidden at their tent in the Vineyards.","rew":"You will learn: Summon Imp\nExperience: 360\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"It was too conspicuous for me to steal the book myself. What luck one of their own patsies did the dirty work for me.","done":"Excellent... I was never able to gain access to this text, it was held in a protected wing of the library that would have looked suspicious for me to be loitering around.\nWell, you did a good job in getting this, and I'm convinced that you can probably handle your own imp, so there's no reason for me not to show you how to summon one.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":49.9,"y":42.6,"n":"Drusilla La Salle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1758":{"id":1758,"t":"Tome of the Cabal","lv":30,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Krom Stoutarm in Ironforge.","desc":"It will take more than a simple summoning circle to bring forth a felhunter for you to challenge.\nMy three acolytes and I will assist in creating the magic circles. You require a copy of the Tome of the Cabal, which has been lost to us for some time. It was written by the first group of warlocks to summon a felhunter unaided.\nPerhaps Krom Stoutarm can help you with this. An itinerant warlock these days, he spends his days hoarding ancient texts and skulking about the library in Ironforge.","rew":"Experience: 600","done":"Tome of Cabal? Hmm...sounds familiar. I have never seen it here before, though--and believe me, I remember every book I read.\nHmm... Ah, yes!\nI have seen reference to it in library cataloging books.\nThe Barrens Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":35.5,"n":"Strahad Farsan","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63,"y":22.6,"n":"Krom Stoutarm","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1678":{"id":1678,"t":"Vejrek","lv":11,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Vejrek's Head to Muren Stormpike in Ironforge.\nVejrek's Head Vejrek","desc":"If you want to rise in the ranks of the warriors, then you better be tough. I can teach you new moves but before that, prove to me you can handle yourself against real foes.\nVejrek is the toughest troll you'll find in these parts, and he's who you have to beat. He has a hut in the foothills just south of Frostmane Hold\nBring me Vejrek's head and I'll know you have mettle.","rew":"Experience: 1,100","back":"Have you been to Vejrek's hut, ‹name›? Is that troll stink I smell on you?","done":"Vejrek sure was an ugly one, eh? Nicely done, ‹name›! You have what it takes, now let's start your lesson...\nYou may not know it, but a strong defense is very important to a warrior. It keeps him standing against foes that'd fell others, and that's what your allies need.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.4,"y":35.6,"n":"Muren Stormpike","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1838":{"id":1838,"t":"Brutal Armor","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring to Thun'grim Firegaze 15 Smoky Iron Ingots, 10 Powdered Azurite, 10 Iron Bars and a Vial of Phlogiston.\n15 Smoky Iron Ingot Windshear Overlord 80 % , Windshear Geomancer 80 % , Windshear Stonecutter 80 % , Windshear Tunnel Rat 80 % and 2 more\n10 Powdered Azurite Hillsbrad Miner 80 %\n10 Iron Bar\nVial of Phlogiston Roogug in Razorfen Kraul\nProvided: Thun'grim's Instructions","desc":"I have heard tales of your strength and valor, and wish to make for you a suit of armor, a companion to aid you as tales of your great deeds grow.\nBut the fashioning of this armor will be a quest unto itself, ‹name›. I will need your help, and the help of other smiths of the Horde.\nHere, take this scroll. I spent many nights, struggling with near-blind eyes, writing that which I need for the armor. Bring me the items on this scroll and I will create for you the first piece of the suit.","rew":"Experience: 3,650","back":"Do you have the items on my scroll, ‹name›?","done":"You brought all that I asked. Now, I will do my part...","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":57.2,"y":30.3,"n":"Thun'grim Firegaze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8798":{"id":8798,"t":"A Yeti of Your Own","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will learn: Tranquil Mechanical Yeti","done":"Say! You know what?! You're an engineer too! So, since you helped me teach my friends a lesson, I'm going to teach you how to make your very own mechanical yeti! Now the fun can go on forever and ever, and you can scare whoever you want! Provided that you can scare up the components to make it that is.\nWhat do you say, ‹name›? Do you want to learn the secret to making a mechanical yeti?","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":60.9,"y":37.6,"n":"Umi Rumplesnicker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]}});